    LLM: 'Game: Tarot. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: 'French Tarot is a trick-taking game for 3â€“5 players (usually 4) using a 78-card deck: 21 numbered trumps (atouts), the Excuse (Fool), and four suits of 14 cards (King, Queen, Knight, Jack, 10â€“1). Six cards form the Dog. Deal 18 each (4-player). Bidding: Petite, Garde, Garde Sans (without Dog), Garde Contre. Taker plays alone vs three defenders. Card points: bouts (21, 1, Excuse) and Kings 4.5 each; Queens 3.5; Knights 2.5; Jacks 1.5; others 0.5. Taker needs 56/51/41/36 points depending on number of Oudlers (bouts) in tricks.',
    objective: 'Taker plays alone vs three defenders. Win enough card points: 56/51/41/36 depending on number of Oudlers (bouts: 21, 1, Excuse) in tricks.',
